# Scaffolded by `lane init` (only when no .gitignore existed) — extend or trim freely.
# Why it ships: vendored deps and local noise must never enter the TDD ledger, and
# `lane start` refuses to claim a task while a vendored dir is untracked and unignored.

# Dependencies — provisioned by setup_cmd in every fresh worktree, never committed.
# Bare names (no trailing slash) so the rule matches even before the dir is created — a
# trailing-slash entry only matches a path git can already see is a directory.
node_modules
vendor
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc

# Build output
dist
build
coverage
target

# Environment / secrets (lane green refuses untracked secret files regardless)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
